# Angular (reservation-frontend)

Apply when editing TypeScript in `reservation-frontend/`.

## Structure
- Place feature-neutral HTTP and API types under `src/app/services/` and `src/app/models/`.
- Keep components thin; call services for backend access.

## HTTP
- Use `HttpClient` from `@angular/common/http` with `provideHttpClient()` in `app.config.ts`.
- Do not hardcode backend URLs in services; read the base URL from `src/environments/environment` (`apiUrl`).

## Environments
- Define `apiUrl` and `production` in `environment.ts` (production build) and `environment.development.ts` (local `ng serve` via `fileReplacements` in `angular.json`).

## Naming
- Use English for code, types, and comments unless the product name is Spanish (e.g. `ReservaService`).

## API alignment
- Match Spring Boot JSON field names (`camelCase` DTOs): e.g. `customerName`, `date`, `time`, `service`, `status`.
